<%#
  Top Up Wallet — the Coinbase-forward funds modal.

  IT IS NO LONGER THE ENTRY BLOCKER'S ANSWER, and this header used to say it was.
  The funds wall now routes to Get USDC (modals/_buy_usdc) via showFundsNeeded,
  because this modal leads with the CDP onramp and that rail has no legal
  clearance (operator, 2026-09-06). selectionBoard#showWalletTopup is kept but has
  no caller; what to do with this modal and the Add Funds hub while the onramp
  stays uncleared is an operator decision about those surfaces, not a modal fix.
  NOTHING OPENS THIS MODAL AT HEAD. Both ways in are closed: showWalletTopup has
  no caller, and the Add Funds hub's Back link (modals/_onramp_hub) swaps here
  only when props.returnModal is 'wallet-topup' — a prop written in exactly one
  place, this file's own "More ways to add funds" link below. So that Back link is
  a return path from itself, not an entrance. An entrance reappears the moment
  either condition changes: something calls showWalletTopup, or some other opener
  passes returnModal: 'wallet-topup'. What follows describes what this modal
  renders and how it gates whenever it IS opened.

  COINBASE-FORWARD (operator 2026-06-13): now that a web2/managed USDC entry
  works (the server signs the on-chain enter_contest with the user's custodial
  key when ENABLE_WEB2_USDC_ENTRY is on), USDC is the cash funding rail again.
  The primary CTA buys USDC with Coinbase (the cdp-ramp buy preflight). There
  are NO entry-token links in the default arrangement; adding tokens or other
  cash rails lives behind the quiet "More ways to add funds" hub (onramp-hub).

  FLAG-AWARE SAFETY (degrade): the kill-switch state (a web2 viewer with
  ENABLE_WEB2_USDC_ENTRY OFF) can NOT pay an entry with USDC, so this modal must
  not pitch "Buy USDC" as their path. The tokenFallback getter (web2 mode AND
  the flag off, read from $store.session) flips the modal to the entry-token
  rail for exactly that audience. web3 and flag-on web2 always see Coinbase.

  The Coinbase rail is server-gated on onramp_rail_visible?(:coinbase), which
  for this rail alone resolves to cdp_ramp_modal_available? — the SAME predicate
  the host layout uses to register the cdp-ramp modal, in every environment. It
  reads logged_in? as well as the ENABLE_CDP_RAMP flag, and both halves matter
  here: this modal is registered UNGATED (it must survive an in-session signup,
  where the server-rendered logged_in? was still false) while cdp-ramp is not,
  so on that page the rail used to outlive its destination. Either half missing
  ships a dead button that swaps to an unregistered cdp-ramp modal.

  One modal id ('wallet-topup'); no internal step machine. The board's
  funds-needed blocker NO LONGER opens it — showFundsNeeded routes to Get USDC or,
  for the USDC kill-switch audience, Buy an Entry Token, and showWalletTopup,
  which held the open/swap pair, has no caller (see the header). The shape it used
  is still the shape any future entrance wants: $store.modals.open('wallet-topup',
  {}) on a cold board, swap() mid-flow.

  Modeled on modals/_onramp_hub + _wallet_deposit. CRITICAL: rendered inside a
  host template x-if, so a SINGLE root element. x-data is a double-quoted
  attribute, so single-quote everything inside the Alpine expressions (the
  getters, the x-text balances, the @click swaps). Each inner template x-if also
  wraps a SINGLE root element.
%>
<div x-data="{
       get props() { return ($store.modals.current() || {}).props || {} },
       get tokenFallback() { return $store.session.mode === 'web2' && !$store.session.web2UsdcEntry },
       get usdcDisplay() { var c = $store.session.usdcCents; return (c === null || c === undefined) ? '—' : '$' + (c / 100).toFixed(2) }
     }"
     class="relative">

  <%# Top-right close. Backdrop close still works too. %>
  <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/close_x" %>

  <div class="text-center pt-1 mb-2">
    <h3 class="text-heading font-bold text-lg leading-tight">Top Up Wallet</h3>
  </div>

  <%# Header balance line. Default: the USDC balance (the funding currency),
      em-dash when the navbar cache is cold. Degrade: the entry-token count for
      the kill-switch (web2 + flag off) audience, who fund with a token. %>
  <p x-show="!tokenFallback" class="text-xs text-body mb-4 text-center">
    USDC balance:
    <span class="font-mono font-semibold text-heading" x-text="usdcDisplay"></span>
  </p>
  <p x-show="tokenFallback" class="text-xs text-body mb-4 text-center">
    Entry tokens:
    <span class="font-mono font-semibold text-heading"
          x-text="($store.session.tokensAvailable | 0)"></span>
  </p>

  <% if onramp_rail_visible?(:coinbase) %>
    <%# PRIMARY (Coinbase-forward) — Buy USDC with Coinbase. swap() (not open)
        because we are already inside the host, and cdp-ramp is its own modal id.
        Hidden for the tokenFallback (web2 kill-switch) audience, where USDC
        can not fund the entry. border-primary marks it as the primary action. %>
    <template x-if="!tokenFallback">
      <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/rail_row",
            emphasis:   :primary,
            on_click:   "$store.modals.swap('cdp-ramp', { flow: 'buy', step: 'preflight' })",
            icon_label: "C",
            icon_bg:    "#0052FF",
            title:      "Buy USDC with Coinbase",
            subtitle:   "Card or bank · funds your entry",
            data:       { topup_rail: "coinbase" } %>
    </template>
  <% end %>

  <%# Token-path degrade — reached ONLY by the web2 kill-switch (web2 mode with
      ENABLE_WEB2_USDC_ENTRY off). USDC can not pay that entry, so the entry
      token is the funding rail. Opens the existing tokens-picker step of the
      auth wizard with the props showTokensPanel uses. %>
  <template x-if="tokenFallback">
    <%# icon_class: "text-xl" — the primitive's default suits LETTERS, and an
        emoji under text-white font-extrabold renders as a fuzzy white blob.
        icon_label is U+1F3AB TICKET, the glyph this tile has always drawn (it
        was &#127915; before the defork). NOT U+1F39F ADMISSION TICKETS, which
        is a different emoji in a different colour and is what the engine's
        _ds_wallet_topup specimen passes — copying the specimen's local instead
        of this app's prior markup is how it got swapped. %>
    <%= render "studio/modals/blocks/rail_row",
          emphasis:   :primary,
          on_click:   "$store.modals.swap('auth', { step: 'tokens-picker', mintedCount: 0, mintedBalance: 0, errorText: '', redirectUrl: '', txSignature: '' })",
          icon_label: "🎫",
          icon_class: "text-xl",
          title:      "Buy Entry Tokens",
          subtitle:   "1 token = 1 contest entry",
          data:       { topup_rail: "tokens" } %>
  </template>

  <%# Quiet link to the Add Funds hub — the other cash rails (PayPal / Venmo /
      Stripe) plus a repeat Coinbase entry. returnModal: 'wallet-topup' tells the
      hub's Back link to slide back HERE rather than to the tokens picker. %>
  <button type="button"
          @click="$store.modals.swap('onramp-hub', { returnModal: 'wallet-topup' })"
          class="block mx-auto mt-4 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-heading transition">
    More ways to add funds &rarr;
  </button>
</div>
